# raglogs — core rules

raglogs analyzes a bounded time window of logs and produces a short,
evidence-backed incident explanation. CLI (Typer) + FastAPI, Python 3.10+,
async SQLAlchemy on Postgres + pgvector. Full detail lives in `AGENTS.md`.

## Pipeline (keep it source-agnostic)

ingest → normalize → fingerprint → cluster → baseline compare → evidence
assembly → explain / timeline / compare. Everything after ingestion is
source-agnostic — new inputs are **adapters** in `src/adapters/` that yield
`ParsedLogLine`, never special cases in core.

## Where things go

- CLI command → `src/cli/commands/` (one file per command)
- API route → `src/api/routes/`
- Normalization / trigger patterns → `src/core/normalization/patterns.py`
- LLM calls → only through `src/core/llm/provider.py`
- Config → env vars via `src/config/settings.py`

## Must

- Type-annotate every function signature. Prefer explicit over clever.
- Keep the `noop` LLM provider working — the tool must run without an API key.
- Add a new Alembic migration; never edit an applied one in `migrations/versions/`.
- `make lint` and `make test-unit` pass before proposing changes.

## Never touch

`.env`, applied migrations, `sample_data/` fixtures, generated artifacts. Never
commit secrets.
